        <h1 class="mb-4">About Me</h1>

        <p>I enjoy problem solving and being around people who do too. That drive led me to join CSUMB's competitive programming team, and shows up outside of CS in the team sports I play and games I run with friends.</p>

        <p>My curiosity is what pulled me into CS — it's a field where you can apply your skills almost anywhere, which matters to me because I don't want to be boxed in. That same curiosity led me to research. I have ADD, and when a problem hits right, that becomes an advantage.</p>

        <p>I'm part of CTI's CSin3 program, an accelerated path to a CS bachelor's in three years between CSUMB and Hartnell College. During my time at Hartnell I worked as a tutor, finishing as lead tutor at the Alisal campus.</p>

        <p>I've also begun my journey of open source contributions — 2 at p5.js and 1 at git-extras so far.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Highlights</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>18th of 73 teams, ICPC Pacific Northwest Regional Division 2 (2025)</li>
            <li>NIH NHGRI GREAT Scholar</li>
            <li>Contributed QOL feature impacting 200K+ monthly users of p5.js Web Editor</li>
            <li>Maintaining 3.5+ GPA in an accelerated bachelor's program while researching</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Skills</h2>
